# What must not go into a build context.
#
# Coolify builds from a git clone, so most of this is already absent there —
# but a build run from a working copy copies the directory as it stands, and
# two of these are worth being explicit about.
#
# data/ is the live database and every uploaded file: subscriber addresses,
# orders, the lot. It is a mounted volume in production and has no business
# being baked into an image that might be pushed to a registry.
#
# node_modules/ carries compiled native binaries — better-sqlite3 and sharp —
# built for whatever Node the developer happens to run. Copied into an image
# running a different Node they fail to load at all, with an ABI mismatch that
# reads as a corrupt install rather than a stale copy.

node_modules
data
.git
.svelte-kit
build
.nixpacks

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

notes
screenshots
*.tar.gz
